    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref> entity bound to the <computeroutput>pharmacies</computeroutput> table (a pharmacy service provider). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A thin value type that binds the generic Service/Entity SQL machinery to one database table. CRUD/search statement generation and staff management are entirely inherited; this class only fixes the table name and exposes it to the permission layer. Instances are built from one of the <ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Types" kindref="compound">api::v2::Types</ref> data wrappers (for example <ref refid="classCreate__t" kindref="compound">Create_t</ref> or <ref refid="classRead__t" kindref="compound">Read_t</ref>), which <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> stores as an <ref refid="entity_8hpp_1aa7ee46136fb273d4151dc647393adcdd" kindref="member">EntityType</ref> variant. The type satisfies the api::v2::Service_t concept and is selected through the <computeroutput>pharmacies</computeroutput> entries of the services and staff route registries (<ref refid="classServiceController" kindref="compound">ServiceController&lt;Pharmacies&gt;</ref>, <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController&lt;Pharmacies&gt;</ref>). Ownership: the wrapper is copied into the base and is const thereafter; no other resources are owned. Instances have no mutable state and do no locking of their own; <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> uses the inherited <ref refid="classService_1ac5c73e3e8d87d1a87af5c12dcee32013" kindref="member">Service::getServicePermissionsQuery</ref> together with <ref refid="classPharmacies_1ac33e2e1e5b9acd10a5a62ff9772e20c7" kindref="member">getTableName()</ref> to authorise staff changes. Copy and move are deleted by <ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref>: construct a fresh instance per operation. <simplesect kind="note"><para>No default constructor: <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> needs a data wrapper to build statements from. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref>, <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="classServiceController" kindref="compound">ServiceController</ref>, <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController</ref>, <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
